  editing.

  [1mThe consequence:[0m [38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m is the only place the field is produced, but [38;5;153mGET /users[39m has documented external
  consumers. Per [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m:

  [2m▎[0m [3mConsumers of [38;5;153mGET /users[39m: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later), and the nightly partner export. Field names in [0m
  [2m▎[0m [3mthe response are part of the contract; changes go through a versioned endpoint.[0m

  Renaming [38;5;153muserId[39m → [38;5;153muser_id[39m in place is a breaking change for all three. The iOS app is the sharpest edge: shipped 3.2+
  clients can't be updated in lockstep, so they'd break until users upgrade. The nightly partner export breaks silently
  — a missing key usually shows up as nulls, not an error. And the README says this class of change is supposed to go
  through a versioned endpoint, which the one-line rename bypasses.

  [1mOptions:[0m

